from pathlib import Path

p = Path('src/hooks/useGame.js')
s = p.read_text()
old = '''ARC COMPLETION — CHECK EVERY MESSAGE, THE PLAYER CANNOT SEE THE ARC. The antagonist above is hidden from the player: they will NOT remind you to close the arc, so missing it silently breaks the game (no new arc can be assigned until you emit the tag). At the end of any message where the antagonist was confronted, fought, negotiated with, or affected, ask: is this antagonist now dead, captured, permanently driven off, dismantled, or otherwise finished as a threat? If YES, [ARC COMPLETE] is MANDATORY in that same message — not next turn, not after an epilogue. The arc is complete when the ANTAGONIST is resolved, even if loose flavor threads remain. RESOLVED HAS TWO FORMS: (a) the antagonist is finished as above, OR (b) the player has concluded their business with the antagonist and disengaged — struck a deal, made a truce, taken their payment and walked away, or otherwise ended the conflict on their own terms. A self-interested player who settles with the antagonist and moves on HAS resolved the arc, even if the antagonist still lives and operates in the world — the story between them is over. Do not force the player to eliminate an antagonist they have chosen to make peace or profit with. Do not wait for the player to wrap up side business, and do not keep a beaten or bought-off antagonist on life support to extend the arc.'''
new = '''ARC COMPLETION — CHECK EVERY MESSAGE, THE PLAYER CANNOT SEE THE ARC. The antagonist above is hidden from the player: they will NOT remind you to close the arc, so missing it silently breaks the game (no new arc can be assigned until you emit the tag). At the end of any message where the antagonist was confronted, fought, negotiated with, or affected, ask: is this antagonist now dead, captured, permanently driven off, dismantled, bought off, allied with, or otherwise finished as the player's active threat? If YES, [ARC COMPLETE] is MANDATORY in that SAME MESSAGE — not next turn and not after an epilogue.

THE ANTAGONIST IS THE HARD BOUNDARY OF THE ARC. ONCE THIS SPECIFIC ANTAGONIST IS RESOLVED, THE ARC ENDS. STOP BUILDING THE ARC IMMEDIATELY. Do NOT reveal that they served a hidden superior. Do NOT invent a mastermind behind them, a larger conspiracy, a revenge faction, a successor villain, a secret organization, a new threat exposed by their defeat, or any other "deeper layer" to keep the same arc going. Do NOT reinterpret their defeat as merely one stage of a larger conflict. Those ideas, if they ever appear at all, belong to a FUTURE ARC after the app assigns one — never to the current arc. You may narrate the IMMEDIATE AFTERMATH of the antagonist's resolution (collapsing lair, freed captives, witnesses reacting, payment, loot, consequences already caused), but those loose ends do NOT delay completion. Emit [ARC COMPLETE] in the resolution message and let the app decide what comes next.

RESOLVED HAS TWO FORMS: (a) the antagonist is finished as a threat — dead, captured, permanently driven off, dismantled, imprisoned, stripped of power, etc.; OR (b) the player has concluded their business with the antagonist and disengaged — struck a deal, made a truce, accepted payment, allied with them, decided they no longer care, or otherwise ended the conflict on their own terms. A self-interested player who settles with the antagonist and moves on HAS resolved the arc, even if the antagonist still lives and operates in the world — the story between them is over. Do not force the player to eliminate an antagonist they have chosen to make peace or profit with. Do not wait for side business to finish, and do not keep a beaten or bought-off antagonist on life support to extend the arc.'''
assert old in s, 'arc completion block not found'
s = s.replace(old, new, 1)
p.write_text(s)
print('arc completion boundary strengthened')
